==Trivia==
*Much like the [[Heal Spirit]], who was the first card to be reworked into a Troop from a Spell, the Furnace is also a first of its kind rework. Only instead it was reworked into a troop from a building.
*In the German, Turkish, Japanese and Finnish language settings of the game, the Furnace's name translates to "Oven". In the Norwegian, Korean, and Chinese language settings of the game, the Furnace's name translates to "Fireplace", "Blast Furnace", and "Furnace of Flames" respectively.
*The Furnace was the first [[:Category:Building Cards|building]] to be added to the game after Clash Royale's release.
*While the current, reworked Furnace is not available as a troop in Clash of Clans, the original version is available as a Dark Elixir troop. 
**The Furnace in Clash of Clans spawns "''Firemites''" instead of Fire Spirits, although one could argue that a Firemite is just a Fire Spirit under a different name.
*The Furnace is 1 of 23 [[cards]] that has had its [[Elixir]] cost changed, the others being [[Bomber]], [[Fire Spirit]], [[Royal Recruits]], [[Cannon]], [[Mortar]], [[Musketeer]], [[Three Musketeers]], [[Heal]], [[Goblin Hut]], [[Bomb Tower]], [[Barbarian Hut]], [[Elixir Collector]], [[Skeleton Army]], [[P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Electro Giant]], [[Bowler]], [[Goblin Barrel]], [[Barbarian Barrel]], [[Rage]], [[Fisherman]], and the [[Monk]].
*The Furnace's description could be a reference towards the [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]] since the Mini P.E.K.K.A says "''pancakes''" when deployed in the [[Arenas|Arena]].
*This may be inspired by a scrapped card idea called the [https://x.com/ClashRoyale/status/1597597818763751424 "Fire Knight"] and he slightly resembles the [https://character-catalogue.fandom.com/wiki/Potter_(Clash) Potter] from Clash Mini.
*The Furnace was featured in the winning [[Battle Decks|deck]] of the [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kIGdeKaT_is The Crown Duel Tournament], by a player called Backstabx.
*The Furnace is the subject of multiple [[Emotes]].

